Hi,

first, congratulations to HP for bringing the first IPP Everywhere 
printers to the market:

http://www.pwg.org/dynamo/eveprinters.php

I am currently on a Canonical (company who makes Ubuntu) sprint having 
several meeting about the development of printing in Ubuntu. The 
conference organization team has usually a printer on their desk and 
this time it is the

HP OfficeJet Pro 8710

one of the IPP Everywhere printers!

I did not help the organization team buying there printer, it was really 
a coincidence, and I discovered it simply by doing printing tests and 
then discovering that cups-browsed has automatically created a print 
queue which sends PWG Raster to the printer. Then I checked the model 
and discovered that it is a nice and shiny IPP Everywhere printer!

Pranjal, the test printout used MuPDF through your GSoC contributions to 
cups-filters, you part is working great here. Thank you very much!

Pictures of the printer and the first IPP-Everywhere-based printouts 
attached. Unfortunately, there is no IPP Everywhere logo neither on the 
printer nor on the box. Note that the too dark printouts under the IPP 
Everywhere printout on the top are printed with CUPS' Deskjet sample PPD.

PPD auto-generated by cups-browsed also attached.

    Till

